Specification CoreTypes

Description The types every other specification in SimpleAccount is written in.
Details Declared once here because the analyzer treats a spec folder as one
Details namespace; the other files refer to these names without redeclaring them.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Money
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DataType Money
Description A signed amount in the currency of the book.
Details Two decimal places, held as whole cents so that sums are exact.
Details A leading dollar sign and thousands separators may be written and are
Details accepted on input; the stored value is the number.
Uses Decimal
Examples: ValidValues
| Value     | IsValid | Notes                              |
| 0.00      | true    | A zero amount is legal             |
| 12.34     | true    |                                    |
| -12.34    | true    | Negative is legal: a credit        |
| $1,234.56 | true    | Currency and separators accepted   |
| ($45.00)  | true    | Accounting parentheses mean -45.00 |
| 1.005     | false   | More than two decimal places       |
| 12.3.4    | false   | Not a number                       |
|           | false   | Empty is not zero                  |
| USD 12.34 | false   | No currency codes in this release  |

BusinessRule Money is held as whole cents
Description Parsing text into a stored integer number of cents.
Details Rounding is not applied: a third decimal place is rejected rather than
Details rounded, so that no cent is ever invented by an import.
Examples: MoneyParse
| Text      | Cents  | Notes                              |
| 0.00      | 0      |                                    |
| 12.34     | 1234   |                                    |
| -12.34    | -1234  |                                    |
| $1,234.56 | 123456 |                                    |
| ($45.00)  | -4500  | Parentheses are the negative sign  |
| .50       | 50     | Leading zero may be omitted        |
| 12        | 1200   | No decimal point means whole units |
| 12.3      | 1230   | One decimal place is tenths        |

Attributes MoneyParse
| Attribute | Type    | Default |
| Text      | String  |         |
| Cents     | Integer | 0       |
| Notes     | String  |         |

BusinessRule Money formats for display
Description How a stored amount is written back out.
Details Negative amounts show a leading minus in the register and parentheses
Details in reports, which is the convention each place is read in.
Examples: MoneyFormat
| Cents  | InRegister | InReport | Notes                    |
| 0      | 0.00     | 0.00     |                            |
| 1234   | 12.34    | 12.34    |                            |
| -1234  | -12.34   | (12.34)  | Two conventions, one value |
| 123456 | 1,234.56 | 1,234.56 | Grouped above a thousand   |

Attributes MoneyFormat
| Attribute | Type    | Default |
| Cents     | Integer | 0       |
| InRegister | String  |         |
| InReport   | String  |         |
| Notes     | String  |         |

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Names and identifiers
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DataType AccountName
Description The name of one account, being one segment of its path.
Details A colon separates the segments of a path, so a name may not contain one.
Details Blanks around a name are trimmed before it is checked, so they can never
Details make a name invalid; " Checking" and "Checking" are the same name.
Uses Text
Examples: ValidValues
| Value         | IsValid | Notes                          |
| Checking      | true    |                                |
| Wells Fargo   | true    | Spaces inside a name are fine  |
| Auto & Travel | true    |                                |
| ~Checking     | true    | Trimmed to Checking            |
|               | false   | A name is required             |
| ~~~           | false   | Blanks alone are no name       |
| Expense:Fuel  | false   | A colon separates segments     |

DataType AccountPath
Description The full colon-separated path of an account, root segment first.
Details This is how every other specification refers to an account.
Uses Text
Examples: ValidValues
| Value              | IsValid | Notes                          |
| Assets:Checking    | true    |                                |
| Expenses:Auto:Fuel | true    | Any depth is allowed           |
| Expenses           | true    | A root account is a valid path |
|                    | false   | A path is required             |
| Expenses:          | false   | Empty trailing segment         |
| :Expenses          | false   | Empty leading segment          |
| Expenses::Fuel     | false   | Empty middle segment           |

DataType PayeeName
Description Who the money went to, or came from.
Details May be empty: a bank fee or an opening balance has no payee.
Uses Text
Examples: ValidValues
| Value         | IsValid | Notes               |
| Harris Teeter | true    |                     |
|               | true    | A payee is optional |
| AT&T          | true    |                     |

DataType Symbol
Description The ticker symbol of a security, where one is known.
Details May be empty. A QIF export carries a security name and often no symbol
Details at all: of the 44 securities in the business file in testdata, not one
Details has a symbol. A holding is identified by its SecurityName, and the
Details symbol is an optional shorthand. See Investments.
Uses Text
Examples: ValidValues
| Value  | IsValid | Notes                               |
| VTSAX  | true    |                                     |
| BRK.B  | true    | A dot is part of some symbols       |
| vtsax  | true    | Folded to upper case on input       |
|        | true    | Unknown; the security has a name    |
| VT SAX | false   | No spaces in a symbol               |

DataType SecurityName
Description The name of a security, which is what a QIF export always gives.
Details Up to 76 characters in the business file in testdata, and all but one
Details of the 44 names contain spaces.
Uses Text
Examples: ValidValues
| Value                          | IsValid | Notes                          |
| ISHARES U S TRANSPORTATION ETF | true    | Spaces are ordinary here       |
| Vanguard Total Stock Mkt Idx   | true    |                                |
| VTSAX                          | true    | A name may look like a symbol  |
|                                | false   | A holding must name a security |

DataType Shares
Description A number of shares or units held.
Details Six decimal places, which is what fund statements report.
Details Never negative: this release does not model short positions.
Uses Decimal
Examples: ValidValues
| Value      | IsValid | Notes                         |
| 0          | true    | A closed position             |
| 100        | true    |                               |
| 12.345678  | true    | Six decimal places            |
| 12.3456789 | false   | Seven is more than is tracked |
| -5         | false   | No short positions            |

DataType Price
Description The price of one share.
Details Four decimal places, never negative.
Uses Decimal
Examples: ValidValues
| Value     | IsValid | Notes                   |
| 0         | true    | Unpriced                |
| 123.4567  | true    | Four decimal places     |
| 123.45678 | false   | Five is too many        |
| -1        | false   | A price is not negative |

DataType CheckNumber
Description The number written on a paper check.
Uses Text
Examples: ValidValues
| Value | IsValid | Notes                       |
| 1234  | true    |                             |
|       | true    | Most transactions have none |
| 1234A | true    | Some banks suffix a letter  |

DataType FitId
Description The identifier a bank assigns a transaction in an OFX file.
Details This is what lets a second import recognise what it has already seen.
Uses Text
Examples: ValidValues
| Value                | IsValid | Notes                        |
| 20240115001          | true    |                              |
| 2024-01-15-AMZN-4499 | true    | Banks choose their own shape |
|                      | false   | Required when OFX supplies it |

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Enumerations
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DataType AccountType
Description What kind of account a node in the tree is.
Details The first six hold money and are reconciled against a statement.
Details Income and Expense are what Quicken calls categories; modelling them as
Details accounts is what makes every transaction balance.
Details Equity holds the opening balances that start the book.
Examples: EnumerationValues
| Value      | Notes                                             |
| Bank       | Checking and savings                              |
| Cash       | A wallet, or petty cash                           |
| CreditCard | A balance owed, which rises as it is spent        |
| Asset      | A house or a car                                  |
| Liability  | A mortgage or a loan                              |
| Investment | Holds securities as well as cash                  |
| Income     | A category money arrives from                     |
| Expense    | A category money goes to                          |
| Equity     | Opening balances, so a new book starts in balance |

DataType AccountClass
Description The two groups the account types fall into.
Details Reports and the balance sheet ask this rather than listing the types.
Examples: EnumerationValues
| Value   | Notes                                                |
| Real    | Bank, Cash, CreditCard, Asset, Liability, Investment |
| Nominal | Income, Expense and Equity: the categories           |

BusinessRule Account class follows from account type
Description Which types are real and which are nominal.
Examples: AccountClassOf
| AccountType | AccountClass | Notes                             |
| Bank        | Real         |                                   |
| Cash        | Real         |                                   |
| CreditCard  | Real         |                                   |
| Asset       | Real         |                                   |
| Liability   | Real         |                                   |
| Investment  | Real         |                                   |
| Income      | Nominal      |                                   |
| Expense     | Nominal      |                                   |
| Equity      | Nominal      | Reconciling it would mean nothing |

Attributes AccountClassOf
| Attribute    | Type         | Default |
| AccountType  | AccountType  | Bank    |
| AccountClass | AccountClass | Real    |
| Notes        | String       |         |

DataType ClearedStatus
Description How far a posting has got through the records of the bank.
Details Held on the posting rather than the transaction, because a transfer
Details between two accounts clears on each statement separately.
Examples: EnumerationValues
| Value      | Notes                                           |
| Uncleared  | Entered here, not yet seen at the bank          |
| Cleared    | Appeared on a downloaded statement              |
| Reconciled | Locked by a finished reconciliation; edits warn |

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One-attribute selectors
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Description A step that names a single value still needs an attribute set, so
Description that the generated code has a struct to carry it. These are those
Description sets: one attribute each, named for what the step selects.
Details The C++ generator emits a typed and a string struct for an Attributes
Details or an Entity block and not for a bare DataType, so a step written as
Details ": AccountPath EveryCell" analyses cleanly and then generates glue that
Details will not compile. These wrappers are the fix.

Attributes AccountSelect
| Attribute | Type        | Default |
| Path      | AccountPath |         |

Attributes HeadingRead
| Attribute | Type    | Default |
| Heading   | Heading |         |

Attributes PayeeSelect
| Attribute | Type      | Default |
| Payee     | PayeeName |         |

Attributes ProfileLabel
| Attribute | Type        | Default |
| Name      | ProfileName |         |

Attributes SearchTerm
| Attribute | Type       | Default |
| Term      | SearchText |         |

Attributes SortBy
| Attribute | Type       | Default |
| Column    | SortColumn |         |

Attributes TransactionSelect
| Attribute | Type           | Default |
| Ref       | TransactionRef |         |
